  "investigation_notes": "Uploads outage is app symptom of `db` dependency down, not storage:\n\n- App `incidentlab-app-1` `running` `Up 4 seconds` then `Up 12 seconds` [E1][E12], inspect `running: true`, `restart_count: 0`, `oom_killed: false` [E5], but `/health` `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` [E2].\n- DB `incidentlab-db-1` `exited` `Exited (0) 2 seconds ago` then `Exited (0) 9 seconds ago` [E1][E12], inspect `running: false`, `status: exited`, `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false` [E6].\n- Storage ruled out as cause:\n  - `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent: 9.0`, `available_mb: 410.6` [E3], `/` `use_percent: 6.8` [E10] \u2014 not full.\n  - `/srv/lab-data/uploads` `app_user_can_write: true`, `owner_uid: 1000` matches `app_uid: 1000` [E4], parent `/srv/lab-data` same `can_write: true` [E11].\n  - App mount `bind source: /srv/lab-data destination: /data rw: true` [E5], same network `incidentlab_default` for both [E5][E6].\n- DB stop looks external clean stop, not crash:\n  - `exit_code: 0` + `die exit_code: 0` + `kill`/`stop` sequence repeated [E6][E9].\n  - `oom_killed: false` [E6].\n  - Was `healthy` via `pg_isready -U lab -d lab exit_code 0` + `health_status: healthy` at `15:58:30` [E9], 3s before `kill/stop/die` at `15:58:33` [E9]; similar pattern `healthy 15:57:49` then `kill 15:57:52` [E9]. Inspect now reports `health: unhealthy` [E6].\n  - App `start 15:58:31` between DB `healthy 15:58:30` and DB `kill 15:58:33` [E9].\n- Why DB was stopped cannot be determined: logs for both containers `unavailable` [E7][E8], events show `kill/stop` actor but not who/why [E9].\n\nConclusion: root cause is `incidentlab-db-1` stopped/exited, app `503` is symptom. Storage permission/disk/mount ruled out. Reason for DB stop = `insufficient_evidence`.\n",
